# Implementation Plan — LearnStudio Auto-TA Multi-Agent Service

This document outlines the architecture, database schema, API design, and frontend implementation plan for the **Auto-TA** service, an automated exam paper generation system powered by a multi-agent orchestration pipeline.

## Architectural Overview

The Auto-TA system is designed as a modular, decoupled set of services inside the LearnStudio platform. It utilizes a **Manager-Worker (Router-Agent) pattern** to coordinate parallel execution, compiler merging, and a human-in-the-loop feedback loop.

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Professor Input] -->|Submit Request| B[Manager Agent / Router]
    B -->|Fan-Out Task| C[Theory Agent]
    B -->|Fan-Out Task| D[Mathematics Agent]
    B -->|Fan-Out Task| E[Question Bank Agent]
    
    C -->|Generate Text/MCQs| F[Editor / Compiler Agent]
    D -->|Generate Numericals| F
    E -->|Fetch Questions| F
    
    F -->|Deduplicate, Verify & Format| G[Professor Review]
    G -->|Approve| H[Final Exam Paper]
    G -->|Reject & Request Revision| I[Feedback Loop]
    I -->|Identify affected agent| B
```

