## Database Schema

We will add the following entities to the database under the `com.learnhub.entity` package to ensure full traceability, versioning, and logging.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    EXAM_REQUEST ||--o{ GENERATED_PAPER : generates
    EXAM_REQUEST ||--o{ AGENT_EXECUTION_LOG : logs
    GENERATED_PAPER ||--o{ GENERATED_QUESTION : contains
    GENERATED_PAPER ||--o{ PAPER_VERSION : has
    GENERATED_PAPER ||--o{ REVIEW_HISTORY : logs
    GENERATED_QUESTION ||--o{ QUESTION_METADATA : tagged-with
```

### 1. `ExamRequest`
Stores the initial parameters submitted by the professor.
- `id` (Long, PK, Auto-increment)
- `subject` (String, nullable=false)
- `course` (String, nullable=false)
- `syllabus` (Text, nullable=false)
- `marks` (Integer, nullable=false)
- `difficulty` (String, nullable=false)
- `questionPattern` (String, nullable=false)
- `totalQuestions` (Integer, nullable=false)
- `status` (Enum: `PENDING`, `RUNNING`, `COMPLETED`, `REJECTED`, `FAILED`)
- `createdAt` (LocalDateTime)

### 2. `GeneratedQuestion`
Stores the questions produced by the agents or retrieved from the bank.
- `id` (Long, PK)
- `questionText` (Text, nullable=false)
- `options` (Text, nullable=true) -- JSON string for MCQ options
- `correctAnswer` (Text, nullable=true)
- `solutionSteps` (Text, nullable=true) -- Step-wise solutions for math questions
- `marks` (Integer, nullable=false)
- `difficulty` (String, nullable=false)
- `questionType` (String) -- MCQ, SHORT, LONG, NUMERICAL
- `agentType` (String) -- THEORY, MATHEMATICS, QUESTION_BANK
- `subject` (String)
- `version` (Integer)

### 3. `QuestionBank`
Stores reusable pre-existing questions in the database.
- `id` (Long, PK)
- `questionText` (Text, nullable=false)
- `options` (Text, nullable=true)
- `correctAnswer` (Text, nullable=true)
- `marks` (Integer, nullable=false)
- `difficulty` (String)
- `questionType` (String)
- `subject` (String)
- `lastUsedAt` (LocalDate, nullable=true)

### 4. `GeneratedPaper`
Represents the combined exam paper.
- `id` (Long, PK)
- `examRequest` (ManyToOne, `ExamRequest`)
- `title` (String, nullable=false)
- `totalMarks` (Integer, nullable=false)
- `status` (Enum: `DRAFT`, `UNDER_REVIEW`, `REVISION_NEEDED`, `APPROVED`, `PUBLISHED`)
- `version` (Integer)
- `fileUrl` (String, nullable=true)
- `createdAt` (LocalDateTime)

### 5. `ReviewHistory`
Traceability logs for reviews.
- `id` (Long, PK)
- `generatedPaper` (ManyToOne, `GeneratedPaper`)
- `action` (Enum: `APPROVE`, `REJECT`, `REQUEST_REGENERATION`)
- `comments` (Text)
- `reviewedAt` (LocalDateTime)

### 6. `AgentExecutionLog`
Real-time console logs for each agent.
- `id` (Long, PK)
- `examRequest` (ManyToOne, `ExamRequest`)
- `agentType` (String) -- MANAGER, THEORY, MATHEMATICS, QUESTION_BANK, EDITOR
- `status` (Enum: `RUNNING`, `SUCCESS`, `FAILED`)
- `executionTimeMs` (Long)
- `logOutput` (Text) -- Detailed trace of steps taken
- `timestamp` (LocalDateTime)

### 7. `PaperVersion`
Stores snapshot history of the paper's questions.
- `id` (Long, PK)
- `generatedPaper` (ManyToOne, `GeneratedPaper`)
- `version` (Integer)
- `questionsJson` (Text) -- Serialized list of question IDs
- `changeReason` (String)
- `timestamp` (LocalDateTime)

